   "id": "few-pictures",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "Only 0 picture(s) on the page (0 photographs, footage or raster images, 0 interface fragments). Drawings in SVG do not count.",
   "fix": "Find real pictures of the subject's world with scripts/assets.mjs (photographs, archival images, maps, engravings, footage), download them to assets/ and give them room: a hero picture, one per section that has a subject, a full-width band. At least four, usually six to twelve."
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "no-footage",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "No video anywhere on the page.",
   "fix": "Look for one honest clip with scripts/assets.mjs --video (the place, the material, the process) and use it as a muted loop with a poster frame. Defend its absence only if no clip fits the subject."
  },
  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "focal-point",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "The first screen has no dominant element: the largest type is 24px (1.7vw) and no single picture holds a third of the viewport.",
   "fix": "Make one thing lead: the headline at display size, or one large picture. A grid of many small pictures is not one thing; in blind tests jurors marked a first screen without a headline down every time. On the strongest studied sites the largest type has a median of 8.4vw.",
   "alsoAt": [
    768
   ]
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "small-title",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "The h1 is 24px (\"Terima Kasih\").",
   "fix": "Set the title at display size, or make the large text of the first screen the h1.",
   "alsoAt": [
    768,
    390
   ]
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "name-only-title",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "The h1 is a bare name (\"Terima Kasih\") and nothing else on the first screen says what this is.",
   "fix": "Keep the name if it leads, and give the line under it (18px or more) the plain words: what it is, for whom, where or when. In the study of 97 Sites of the Day, first screens that named nothing lost usability and content points.",
   "alsoAt": [
    768,
    390
   ]
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "hero-void",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "33% of the first screen is one empty block (540×780px at 900,120).",
   "fix": "Place the void on purpose or fill it: move the picture, the film or one fact into it, grow the headline to meet it, or shrink the screen to its content. A void reads as placed only when something closes it on the far side and it is the screen's one rest."
  },
